# Optional: set this to use a real persistent Postgres database for the
# shared leaderboard instead of the built-in JSON-file store (which only
# persists on hosts with a writable filesystem at runtime). Any standard
# Postgres connection string works, including free hosted options like
# Neon, Supabase, or Railway — most of those require SSL, so use the
# connection string they give you as-is (it usually already includes
# ?sslmode=require).
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own value; .env.local is
# git-ignored so your credentials never get committed.
DATABASE_URL=
